{"strongs": "H8460", "word": "ᵑ7", "translit": "te.chot", "root": "", "morph": "A:Prep", "pos": "preposition", "gloss": "under", "definition": "תְּחוֺת preposition under (Biblical Hebrew תַּחַתּ ; ᵑ7 תְּחוֺת , Syriac , , adverb ; Palmyrene מן לתחת Cooke 320 ); — Dan 7:27 תְּחוֺת כָּלשְֿׁמַיָּא (compare Biblical Hebrew II. 1 ); in plural with suffix (as Biblical Hebrew, Syriac, ᵑ7 ) Dan 4:9 תְּחֹתֹהִי (so ᵑ7 Onk Lev 15:10 : Dalm § 47, 2 ), v Lev 15:18 . With מִן , Jer 10:11 מִן תְּחוֺת שְׁמַיָּא (compare Biblical Hebrew III. 2 ); suffix Dan 4:11 מִןתַּֿחְתּוֺהִי (the form as Syriac adverb above, unless a Hebraizing punct.).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9998')\">BDB9998</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H8460')\">H8460</entry> <entry onclick=\"sn('H8478')\">H8478</entry> <entry onclick=\"sn('H8479')\">H8479</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9997')\">BDB9997</entry> | BIBLICAL ARAMAIC | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB9999')\">BDB9999</entry></div><p> <bdbarc>תְּחוֺת</bdbarc> <b>preposition</b> <highlightword>under</highlightword> (Biblical Hebrew <bdbarc>תַּחַתּ</bdbarc>; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <bdbarc>תְּחוֺת</bdbarc>, Syriac <placeholder6189/>, <placeholder6190/>, adverb <placeholder6191/>; Palmyrene <bdbarc>מן לתחת</bdbarc> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Cooke')\">Cooke<sup>320</sup></lookup>); — <ref ref=\"Dan 7:27\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"27\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"27\" onclick=\"bcv(27,7,27)\">Dan 7:27</ref> <bdbarc>תְּחוֺת כָּלשְֿׁמַיָּא</bdbarc> (compare Biblical Hebrew <b>II. 1</b>); in plural with suffix (as Biblical Hebrew, Syriac, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup>) <ref ref=\"Dan 4:9\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(27,4,9)\">Dan 4:9</ref> <bdbarc>תְּחֹתֹהִי</bdbarc> (so <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb><sup><b>Onk</b></sup></looku